# Docker build-context exclusions, shared by every Tablemate image.
#
# Each Dockerfile builds with the repository root as its context (`context: .` in
# docker-compose.yml), so this file governs all of them. Manifests, the lockfile,
# pnpm-workspace.yaml (its overrides and patchedDependencies), patches/,
# tsconfig.base.json, every workspace's sources, config/ and infra/nginx/ stay in the
# context: the images install the workspace and compile it themselves.

# Version control, editors and OS metadata
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets and local state. An env file is excluded at the root or inside a workspace,
# at any depth, and only the documented template is ever sent to a builder.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
.local

# Host installs, compiler output and test reports, from the root or any workspace
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.tsbuild
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.log

# Proving artefacts. The api image carries verification_key.json and no proving key,
# circuit WASM or witness generator, so no context ever holds one: containers receive
# them only through the compose bind mounts (api: verification_key.json and the
# manifest; artifacts: the circuit build directory).
packages/circuits/build
packages/circuits/samples
**/*.ptau
**/*.zkey

# Mobile native and Expo output, regenerated by `expo prebuild` and build-native.sh
apps/mobile/.expo
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/dist
apps/mobile/web-build
apps/mobile/modules/tablemate-prover/rust/target
apps/mobile/modules/tablemate-prover/ios/Frameworks
apps/mobile/modules/tablemate-prover/ios/Generated
apps/mobile/modules/tablemate-prover/android/src/main/jniLibs
apps/mobile/modules/tablemate-prover/android/build
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.ipa

# Host-only material no image reads: documentation, end-to-end specs, the menu
# evaluation fixtures and the k6 script, all of which run on the host
docs
apps/mobile/e2e
apps/workers/eval/fixtures
infra/k6

# Run-harness output kept beside the checkout (screenshots and screen recordings),
# which no image reads
blitzy
